// Text helpers written in Yashy (M6 Task 10).
//
// The string surface is methods now: `len`, `byte_at`, `slice`, `trim`,
// `contains`, `starts_with`, `split` and the rest are called on a string
// binding. The wrappers this module used to export were removed in M12 so
// there is one spelling per operation. What remains is `concat`, a named
// spelling for `+` that reads well in a pipeline of stdlib helpers.
//
// Graphemes (Phase 6) are methods too, on the same binding:
// `graphemes()` counts clusters, `char_at(i)` returns the cluster at `i`,
// and `substring(start, end)` returns the clusters in a clamped range.
// `len()` keeps counting bytes; a byte index and a grapheme index are
// different functions, never overloads of one name.

// Ownership: a fresh string is returned; neither argument is consumed.
pub fn concat(string left, string right) -> string {
    return left + right;
}
